assets.prompt:
Use case: stylized-concept.
Asset type: production TRANSPARENT architecture sprite atlas for a playable 2.5D isometric Chinese cultivation village, Wang Family Village.
Primary request: exactly THREE equal columns and TWO equal rows on a landscape 3:2 canvas, six independent complete sprites. Real transparent alpha background throughout the empty areas and between sprites.
Style: refined hand-painted fantasy RPG environment, believable humble old Chinese village architecture, blue charcoal ceramic roofs, warm ivory plaster and aged timber, restrained amber lanterns, moss and tiny pink flowers. Consistent 2:1 isometric orthographic view from above looking toward north, vertical walls upright, horizontal ground axes at ±26.6 degrees. The same architecture perspective and morning light from upper left in every cell. Clearly readable silhouettes and crisp roof details.
Order left to right, top to bottom:
1. Wang family home: wide modest one-storey cottage with blue tiled gabled roof, open wooden porch on the SOUTH-facing visible front, warm window, small tan sack and clay jar close to wall;
2. apothecary cottage: one-storey blue tile roof house, small herb drying racks and brown baskets neatly against the front wall, ivory plaster, warm window; NO sign lettering;
3. scholar's small timber cottage with a blue tiled roof and a little open porch, bamboo lattice window and a closed scroll on a table against wall;
4. village stone well: circular gray stone rim, timber crossbeam, small tiled roof, wooden bucket and rope, compact square ground footprint;
5. carpenter workbench: low long wooden table with plank, mallet and wood shavings, a small stacked timber rack behind it, no roof;
6. small ancestral wayside shrine: compact gray stone and timber shrine with blue tile roof, plain unlettered plaque, two tiny amber lanterns.
Composition: each object centered within its own exact square cell with at least 8% fully transparent margin; feet/base on same baseline at 90% cell height. Every roof and prop fully visible inside its cell. No large landscape platform beneath any object. No ground tiles, no scenery, no people, no UI, no words, no text, no labels, no watermark, no black background or checkerboard. Very faint tight contact shadow only, keep surrounding alpha clear.

Use case: stylized-concept.
Asset type: production transparent nature/utility sprite atlas for the same playable 2.5D isometric Chinese village as the architecture atlas.
Primary request: exactly THREE equal columns and TWO equal rows on a landscape 3:2 image; six complete separate sprites; actual transparent alpha outside all objects.
Style: premium hand-painted Chinese fantasy village, natural detailed painted leaves and wood, calm warm morning sun from upper left, moss green, soft peach-pink and blue-charcoal accents, consistent 2:1 orthographic isometric camera with ground axes at ±26.6 degrees. Each sprite should be readable at 100–250 pixels tall.
Exact order left to right top to bottom:
1. tall beautiful willow tree with curving dark trunk, draping narrow green leaves, sparse pale green highlights, trunk foot visible;
2. broad small peach blossom tree, warm gray trunk and airy clusters of pale pink flowers, no giant glow;
3. simple rustic timber footbridge with side rails and six pale weathered planks spanning along the isometric +x axis, from UPPER LEFT to LOWER RIGHT at +26.6 degrees on the canvas. Entire bridge including both ends visible, shallow bridge rise, no roof, no water or terrain under it;
4. short rustic wooden fence segment with three posts and two rails, moss at base, along an isometric ground axis;
5. low broad garden bed of leafy medicinal herbs with small pale blue flowers and a few gray stones at its edge, compact ground-level sprite;
6. a timber village lantern post with one hanging amber lantern, dark old wood, small stone footing, NO huge glow circle.
Each square cell has at least 8% empty alpha around the complete object. Center object and put base near 90% of the cell's height. No scenery, no people, no labels, no words or writing, no UI, no borders, no platforms, no black rectangles, no visible checkerboard. Preserve true alpha and clear gaps between leaves.

Use case: stylized-concept.
Asset type: six-material opaque texture atlas for the ground of a playable hand-painted 2.5D Chinese village.
Primary request: exactly THREE columns and TWO rows, six precisely aligned SQUARE material patches, no gaps or borders. Landscape 3:2 canvas. These are TOP DOWN flat texture swatches, no perspective or objects. Each cell is a continuous repeatable material, with edges designed to tile gently.
Order left to right top to bottom:
1. soft mossy meadow grass, natural muted sage and olive green, very sparse tiny warm beige specks, no large flowers;
2. weathered village stone paving, irregular small flat warm-gray and tan cobblestones with tiny moss in joints, subtle worn variation, no huge cracks;
3. smooth pale brown packed-earth lane, fine dust and tiny embedded pebbles, subtle low-contrast texture;
4. calm shallow jade-turquoise stream water, small delicate horizontal painted ripples and sparse soft sun reflections, NO shore, NO rocks;
5. dark fertile garden soil in subtle rows with a few tiny short green seedlings, no large plant objects;
6. pale natural riverbank gravel, small rounded warm-gray pebbles and patches of muted olive moss, NO stream or large rocks.
Medium: polished hand-painted RPG game texture, fine painterly detail, soft morning ambient light, low contrast, balanced cohesive natural palette. No dramatic lighting baked in, no cast shadows, no text, no symbols, no scenes, no UI, no characters, no 3D blocks, no grids, no watermark. These six flat swatches must cover their entire cells and meet exact 1/3 width and 1/2 height boundaries.
